    <script type="application/ld+json">{"mainEntity":{"headline":"Arsenate ions Remediation from Contaminated Water Upon Interaction with Novel ZnO-CuO Nanocomposite with Ficus Carica Biochar","description":"The current investigation explored the ability of a novel nanocomposite (NC) of Ficus carica biochar (FCB) with zinc oxide and copper oxide (FCB-ZnO-CuO NC) to remove arsenate ions from polluted water, an environmentally harmful contaminant, using a batch technique. The presence of prominent peaks of ZnO and CuO was detected using EDX and FTIR techniques, while the morphology and particle size were determined by TEM and SEM. SEM shows irregular morphology of FCB-ZnO-CuO, and TEM shows an average particle size of 11.52 nm. XRD analysis validated the average particle size and main phases of ZnO and CuO in the composite, and confirmed the crystallinity. The chemical composition and oxidation states of FCB-ZnO-CuO NC were confirmed through XPS analysis, where 1043.20 eV and 1020 eV validate Zn, and 952.07 eV and 932.16 eV confirm the presence of Cu. The PZC of FCB-ZnO-CuO was observed at 8.50. The adsorption results revealed that under conditions of 80 mg As L-1, pH 6, a dosage of 0.5 g, and a temperature of 318 K, the FCB-ZnO-CuO NC exhibited maximum arsenate ion removal (94.65%). A reusability study showed a decline in arsenate ion adsorption from 97.02% to 40.33% in five cycles. The best fit (R2 > 0.98) was determined by the Langmuir isotherm, while the pseudo-second-order model effectively explains the kinetics of arsenate ion adsorption (R2 > 0.99).","datePublished":"2026-09-15T00:00:00Z","dateModified":"2026-09-15T00:00:00Z","pageStart":"1","pageEnd":"21","sameAs":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11270-026-09954-8","keywords":["Biochar","Adsorption","Zinc oxide","Copper oxide","Environment","general","Water Quality/Water Pollution","Atmospheric Protection/Air Quality Control/Air Pollution","Soil Science & Conservation","Hydrogeology","Climate Change/Climate Change Impacts"],"image":["https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11270-026-09954-8/MediaObjects/11270_2026_9954_Sch1_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11270-026-09954-8/MediaObjects/11270_2026_9954_Fig1_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11270-026-09954-8/MediaObjects/11270_2026_9954_Fig2_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11270-026-09954-8/MediaObjects/11270_2026_9954_Fig3_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11270-026-09954-8/MediaObjects/11270_2026_9954_Fig4_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11270-026-09954-8/MediaObjects/11270_2026_9954_Fig5_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11270-026-09954-8/MediaObjects/11270_2026_9954_Fig6_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11270-026-09954-8/MediaObjects/11270_2026_9954_Fig7_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11270-026-09954-8/MediaObjects/11270_2026_9954_Fig8_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11270-026-09954-8/MediaObjects/11270_2026_9954_Fig9_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11270-026-09954-8/MediaObjects/11270_2026_9954_Fig10_HTML.png"],"isPartOf":{"name":"Water, Air, & Soil Pollution","issn":["1573-2932","0049-6979"],"volumeNumber":"237","@type":["Periodical","PublicationVolume"]},"publisher":{"name":"Springer International Publishing","logo":{"url":"https://www.springernature.com/app-sn/public/images/logo-springernature.png","@type":"ImageObject"},"@type":"Organization"},"author":[{"name":"Sana Shakil","affiliation":[{"name":"University of Azad Jammu and Kashmir","address":{"name":"Department of Chemistry, University of Azad Jammu and Kashmir, Muzaffarabad, Pakistan","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"@type":"Person"},{"name":"Salah Ud Din","affiliation":[{"name":"University of Azad Jammu and Kashmir","address":{"name":"Department of Chemistry, University of Azad Jammu and Kashmir, Muzaffarabad, Pakistan","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"email":"salah.mahsud@uajk.edu.pk","@type":"Person"},{"name":"Khawaja Ansar Yasin","affiliation":[{"name":"University of Azad Jammu and Kashmir","address":{"name":"Department of Chemistry, University of Azad Jammu and Kashmir, Muzaffarabad, Pakistan","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"@type":"Person"},{"name":"Muhammad Sheraz Ahmad","affiliation":[{"name":"Kocaeli University","address":{"name":"Department of Environmental Engineering, Kocaeli University, Izmit, Kocaeli, Türkiye","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"@type":"Person"},{"name":"Muhammad Imran","affiliation":[{"name":"Gdansk University of Technology","address":{"name":"Faculty of Civil and Environmental Engineering, Department of Sanitary Engineering, Gdansk University of Technology, Gdansk, Poland","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"},{"name":"COMSATS University Vehari Campus","address":{"name":"Department of Environmental Sciences, COMSATS University Vehari Campus, Vehari, Pakistan","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"@type":"Person"},{"name":"Jamoliddin Razzokov","affiliation":[{"name":"National Research University-TIIAME","address":{"name":"Institute of Fundamental and Applied Research, National Research University-TIIAME, Tashkent, Uzbekistan","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"},{"name":"Karshi State Technical University","address":{"name":"Department of Natural Sciences, Karshi State Technical University, Kashkadarya, Uzbekistan","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"},{"name":"Tashkent State Tec